3,"open_issues":2724,"watchers":15335,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"### Describe the bug\n\nThe quarkus configuration documentation states that the configuration parameter: `quarkus.http.test-timeout` can be used to set the timeout for the REST Assured HTTP client [here](https://quarkus.io/guides/all-config)\nHowever, if you set this parameter and run tests using `quarkus build` you get the warning:\n`2025-11-17 15:30:53,973 WARN  [io.qua.config] (main) Unrecognized configuration key \"quarkus.http.test-timeout\" was provided; it will be ignored; verify that the dependency extension for this configuration is set or that you did not make a typo`\nThis bug has been reported before in a much earlier version of quarkus [here](https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/15859)\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe configuration parameter is accepted and the HTTP timeout configured per the docs\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nA warning is generated (see above) and the timeout is not applied.\n\n### How to Reproduce?\n\nQuickest way to reproduce is to check out the first project from https://quarkus.io/guides/getting-started\nIn the src/test/resources/application.properties file add:\n`quarkus.http.test-timeout=120s` \nRun `quarkus build`\n\n### Output of `uname -a` or `ver`\n\nDarwin Bruces-MacBook-Pro.local 25.1.0 Darwin Kernel Version 25.1.0: Mon Oct 20 19:34:05 PDT 2025; root:xnu-12377.41.6~2/RELEASE_ARM64_T6041 arm64\n\n### Output of `java -version`\n\nOpenJDK Runtime Environment (build 23.0.1+11-39) OpenJDK 64-Bit Server VM (build 23.0.1+11-39, mixed mode, sharing)\n\n### Quarkus version or git rev\n\n3.28.3\n\n### Build tool (ie. output of `mvnw --version` or `gradlew --version`)\n\nApache Maven 3.9.10 (5f519b97e944483d878815739f519b2eade0a91d)\n\n### Additional information\n\n_No response_","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/51061/reactions","total_c